Kostadis Roussos: slaughtering monsters, at least with normal adventures, they slaughter a monster and take its treasures. These ones slaughter a monster and move on, or donate it to some charity in which they again tried to do good.

425
00:37:59.700 --> 00:38:00.710
Kostadis Roussos: They're always….

426
00:38:00.710 --> 00:38:04.770
Gary Young: I mean, like, all that good, good treasure.

427
00:38:06.340 --> 00:38:07.340
Kostadis Roussos: They're, they're….

428
00:38:07.340 --> 00:38:10.169
David Mendenhall: committed to neutrality. Really committed.

429
00:38:10.170 --> 00:38:12.530
Wade: So beautiful, yet so neutral.

430
00:38:12.880 --> 00:38:17.460
Kostadis Roussos: She's like, they are… they are… theirs is a path of madness.

431
00:38:17.950 --> 00:38:19.120
David Mendenhall: Madness.

432
00:38:19.510 --> 00:38:30.459
Kostadis Roussos: Yes, is it not mad to not see that the universe itself, the multiverse itself, is one thing? That there isn't good, and there isn't evil, there's just the thing?

433
00:38:31.910 --> 00:38:37.539
Kostadis Roussos: And that she is… and that the order of the gauntlet is committed to its path?

434
00:38:38.590 --> 00:38:41.990
Kostadis Roussos: I… Soma understands this, and I thought you did.

435
00:38:41.990 --> 00:38:46.980
David Mendenhall: Some of you understand that there's… There's neither good nor evil.

436
00:38:47.350 --> 00:38:51.650
Wade: I understand that all things are, you know… Temporary.

437
00:38:53.970 --> 00:39:09.059
Kostadis Roussos: I did not say there's no such thing as a good act or an evil act, but the idea that by striving, one can force the world to be better, good or evil. Well, one can do that, but what happens is that the evil will then have to respond, and it won't respond

438
00:39:09.060 --> 00:39:22.140
Kostadis Roussos: Gently, it will respond with full force. The more you push in one direction, the bigger the reaction in the other direction is. And isn't our goal to maintain the symbiosis of the multiverse? Instead, what happens is the worlds fall apart.

439
00:39:24.950 --> 00:39:27.329
David Mendenhall: Maybe we really should have left you in that house.

440
00:39:28.800 --> 00:39:31.550
Wade: Oh, you do not like her.

441
00:39:31.550 --> 00:39:34.540
David Mendenhall: Well, I mean, why did we go save her?

442
00:39:34.860 --> 00:39:38.939
David Mendenhall: Per 50 GP? She doesn't want… she doesn't want good.

443
00:39:38.940 --> 00:39:45.699
Kostadis Roussos: She goes, she pauses and says, my dear friend, Vukradin.

444
00:39:46.100 --> 00:39:50.169
Kostadis Roussos: As you recall, I wish to be left alone in my house, but you insisted…

445
00:39:50.890 --> 00:39:58.030
Kostadis Roussos: You did insist I come here, and then when you asked for more money from Harbin, did I not intervene to get you more money?

446
00:39:58.630 --> 00:39:59.670
David Mendenhall: You did.

447
00:39:59.670 --> 00:40:03.999
Kostadis Roussos: Yes, and weren't the… and why did I do this? Because….

448
00:40:04.000 --> 00:40:05.450
David Mendenhall: Why did we do it?

449
00:40:05.700 --> 00:40:12.790
Kostadis Roussos: Because this was… this is not about good or evil, it's about seeing balance, and I saw the balance of your just cause.

450
00:40:15.190 --> 00:40:18.839
Kostadis Roussos: You are devoted to music. You are not devoted to

451
00:40:18.960 --> 00:40:24.510
Kostadis Roussos: changing evil or changing harm. Music is part of the music of the universe.

452
00:40:26.470 --> 00:40:28.010
Kostadis Roussos: You are not a…

453
00:40:28.160 --> 00:40:33.640
Kostadis Roussos: A devotee of the powers of good, or even the devotee of the powers of evil.

454
00:40:34.210 --> 00:40:34.740
Gary Young: Music.

455
00:40:34.740 --> 00:40:35.139
David Mendenhall: I'm good.

456
00:40:36.660 --> 00:40:44.110
Kostadis Roussos: So, I thought, I thought of someone who was so passionate about music, that you would see the world as Soma and I do.

457
00:40:45.010 --> 00:40:51.310
Kostadis Roussos: Instead, I notice by your choice of alliances that you see things very differently than me.

458
00:40:53.830 --> 00:40:57.140
David Mendenhall: Okay, I'm done talking to her. She's being patronizing.

459
00:40:59.890 --> 00:41:00.850
David Mendenhall: See ya.

460
00:41:01.930 --> 00:41:09.989
Kostadis Roussos: She goes, very well. I hope… I hope you… I hope you'll take care of the issues of the Whispering Grove, otherwise the things will get worse.

461
00:41:11.570 --> 00:41:12.369
Wade: I'll work on him.

462
00:41:12.370 --> 00:41:15.730
David Mendenhall: I don't know. Maybe we shouldn't disturb the natural order.

463
00:41:19.580 --> 00:41:22.589
Wade: The natural order is actively being disturbed.

464
00:41:22.760 --> 00:41:24.789
Kostadis Roussos: Exactly, says the Adabra.

465
00:41:25.510 --> 00:41:28.690
Kostadis Roussos: It is act… it is actively being disturbed.

466
00:41:29.250 --> 00:41:32.199
Wade: I just like to know who's doing it when we get a chance.

467
00:41:33.060 --> 00:41:42.449
Kostadis Roussos: Nope. So… … alright, so Adabra looks at you and says, could I sell you any potions of healing?

468
00:41:46.470 --> 00:41:48.350
Wade: I think we're alright.

469
00:41:48.350 --> 00:41:52.670
Kostadis Roussos: Well then, if you need anything from me, I will just be over here. Alright.

470
00:41:57.150 --> 00:41:58.300
Gary Young: Okay.

471
00:41:58.720 --> 00:42:00.269
Kostadis Roussos: So, where else do you want to go?

472
00:42:03.550 --> 00:42:05.599
Gary Young: Do we have any treasure to sell?

473
00:42:07.060 --> 00:42:08.980
Wade: There's some octopus hide armor, right?

474
00:42:08.980 --> 00:42:24.979
David Mendenhall: I think, I would like to invest… I would like to talk to some shopkeepers about all of this blood loot we found, and is there a way to identify… are there, like, markings on it that would indicate where it came from, or…

475
00:42:26.180 --> 00:42:33.989
David Mendenhall: Maybe we should… are there any markings that indicate any sort of points of origin, or anything like that that could be helpful?

476
00:42:38.190 --> 00:42:42.569
Kostadis Roussos: I mean, they all turn to you and say, that's what identify spells are for.

477
00:42:42.570 --> 00:42:43.180
Wade: Hmm.

478
00:42:43.510 --> 00:42:45.640
David Mendenhall: Okay, where's some of those?

479
00:42:46.000 --> 00:42:50.610
Kostadis Roussos: She couldn't go, I… you need to go find a magic user for one of those.

480
00:42:53.270 --> 00:42:54.949
Wade: Can we just get some scrolls?

481
00:42:55.850 --> 00:43:11.900
Kostadis Roussos: And LionShield Coaster says, well, I don't happen to have some identify scrolls today, but if you give me a few days, I could probably… I could probably dig some up, or at least find you a bead on someone who could do it, or find you the name of a magic user who could help.

482
00:43:12.270 --> 00:43:19.430
David Mendenhall: Probably we're going to need a magic user who's willing to… Do this pro bono?

483
00:43:19.600 --> 00:43:24.399
David Mendenhall: I don't know to pay a lot of money? To teach Corbin to….

484
00:43:24.400 --> 00:43:26.539
Wade: You identify scrap spells.

485
00:43:26.540 --> 00:43:31.619
Kostadis Roussos: Or, or, or, or, or, you know, you could go talk to your, friend, the, …

486
00:43:32.250 --> 00:43:34.559
Kostadis Roussos: Ser Kaelen, the, ….

487
00:43:34.560 --> 00:43:36.839
David Mendenhall: or Karen, who betrayed me? I don't know.

488
00:43:36.840 --> 00:43:38.280
Kostadis Roussos: Not a big time.

489
00:43:38.280 --> 00:43:39.090
David Mendenhall: Right now.

490
00:43:39.090 --> 00:43:40.820
Kostadis Roussos: Do you know whether he betrayed you?

491
00:43:41.090 --> 00:43:43.770
David Mendenhall: I… suspect that he did.

492
00:43:50.480 --> 00:43:52.870
Wade: … You don't want to confront him about it?

493
00:43:53.340 --> 00:43:55.650
David Mendenhall: Well, he's not here, right? Didn't he leave town?

494
00:43:55.650 --> 00:43:56.759
Kostadis Roussos: No, no, he stayed in town.

495
00:43:56.760 --> 00:43:57.610
Wade: You said town.

496
00:43:58.830 --> 00:44:00.159
Kostadis Roussos: Yeah, Corbin just….

497
00:44:00.160 --> 00:44:01.770
Gary Young: Multiclass send to a wizard.

498
00:44:05.220 --> 00:44:05.980
Kostadis Roussos: Who did?

499
00:44:07.950 --> 00:44:10.109
Gary Young: We should have Corbin multi-class into a wizard.

500
00:44:10.110 --> 00:44:13.999
Wade: Orc. Yeah, so we can do our, our, identify spells.

501
00:44:14.260 --> 00:44:14.620
Gary Young: Yes.

502
00:44:15.130 --> 00:44:19.590
David Mendenhall: He's a lackey that hangs out at camp and casts buff spells on us.

503
00:44:19.590 --> 00:44:20.530
Kostadis Roussos: That's right, that's right.

504
00:44:22.070 --> 00:44:24.349
Wade: Don't underestimate his contribution.

505
00:44:24.660 --> 00:44:27.379
Kostadis Roussos: Do not underestimate his contribution.

506
00:44:28.760 --> 00:44:29.780
Kostadis Roussos: Alright.

507
00:44:30.170 --> 00:44:37.730
Kostadis Roussos: Okay, so, … where would you like to go… would you like to go to the tavern?

508
00:44:38.790 --> 00:44:44.970
David Mendenhall: Was there any sort of… was there anyone… who gave us the quest for the Tower of Storms?

509
00:44:44.970 --> 00:44:48.299
Kostadis Roussos: Nobody gave you the quest for the Tower of Storms, you heard a rumor and you followed it.

510
00:44:48.760 --> 00:44:49.260
David Mendenhall: Okay.

511
00:44:49.260 --> 00:44:50.649
Wade: Doesn't sound like us.

512
00:44:51.530 --> 00:44:53.410
Gary Young: Well, I… it…

513
00:44:54.870 --> 00:45:05.799
Gary Young: It does seem like you should still tell the, the town keeper, because he will need to, you know, see if he wants to keep the, the lighthouse, stocked and….

514
00:45:06.190 --> 00:45:13.509
David Mendenhall: Oh, that's a good point. Yeah, keep the fire going, maybe appoint a new master of the lighthouse to take care of it.

515
00:45:13.510 --> 00:45:15.619
Gary Young: They need to hire a light keeper.

516
00:45:17.670 --> 00:45:18.090
David Mendenhall: We do.

517
00:45:18.090 --> 00:45:19.729
Gary Young: Glorious Lightkeeper.

518
00:45:21.030 --> 00:45:21.610
Kostadis Roussos: Great.

519
00:45:21.610 --> 00:45:23.810
David Mendenhall: Alright, that's a good idea, that's a good idea.

520
00:45:24.990 --> 00:45:25.810
Kostadis Roussos: Hold on that.

521
00:45:27.520 --> 00:45:32.230
Kostadis Roussos: I love it. Alright, so to Court Harbin Master.

522
00:45:32.640 --> 00:45:33.680
Kostadis Roussos: to Harbin.

523
00:45:34.490 --> 00:45:39.490
Kostadis Roussos: He's like… Harbin, … Sarban sees you guys, and is like, well!

524
00:45:39.490 --> 00:45:42.719
Gary Young: What a wonderful… what a wonderful surprise to see you all!

525
00:45:45.550 --> 00:45:53.059
Gary Young: Yeah, … Talos? Did you realize there was an infestation of Talos in, you know, like, on the coast?

526
00:45:56.310 --> 00:46:00.660
Kostadis Roussos: He looks at you funny. We have dragons, and now we have Talos?

527
00:46:02.370 --> 00:46:04.399
Kostadis Roussos: Oh, that's… that's quite awful.

528
00:46:05.290 --> 00:46:07.319
Kostadis Roussos: That is… that is very awful.

529
00:46:07.510 --> 00:46:10.190
Gary Young: But we did sanctify the altar.

530
00:46:10.510 --> 00:46:11.059
Gary Young: No marks.

531
00:46:11.060 --> 00:46:11.780
Kostadis Roussos: You did?

532
00:46:12.020 --> 00:46:12.700
Gary Young: Yes.

533
00:46:13.070 --> 00:46:14.160
Kostadis Roussos: Oh, excellent.

534
00:46:15.040 --> 00:46:17.340
Kostadis Roussos: And so, there's no more Talos.

535
00:46:17.610 --> 00:46:18.889
Gary Young: Yeah, no more talents.

536
00:46:19.200 --> 00:46:22.580
David Mendenhall: Well, no, but we need to go investigate in Leilan.

537
00:46:23.130 --> 00:46:25.549
David Mendenhall: There's… there's more going on there.

538
00:46:25.970 --> 00:46:27.829
Gary Young: Well, not at the White House.

539
00:46:28.390 --> 00:46:33.740
David Mendenhall: Yeah, the lighthouse is good, but Leylon… the Talos worship may continue.

540
00:46:34.820 --> 00:46:41.010
Gary Young: Oh. But there's no one working the lighthouse, so the light will eventually go out. And light is important.

541
00:46:42.190 --> 00:46:42.880
Kostadis Roussos: Yes.

542
00:46:44.710 --> 00:46:46.710
Kostadis Roussos: …

543
00:46:50.940 --> 00:47:06.979
Kostadis Roussos: Harbin goes, I think Lord Neverwinter will be delighted to find out that you have managed to cleanse the lighthouse of the evildoers who had taken ownership of it, and I will make sure to send him a note.

544
00:47:09.370 --> 00:47:11.609
Gary Young: Thank you. Make sure you put in a good word for us.

545
00:47:11.900 --> 00:47:14.249
Kostadis Roussos: I will absolutely put in a great resource.

546
00:47:14.250 --> 00:47:16.599
David Mendenhall: to Neverwinter and take it to him personally?

547
00:47:18.530 --> 00:47:31.310
Kostadis Roussos: You could, I suppose. I don't know whether he'd want to see you, but he's a very busy man. If this is something you wish to do, far be it for me to say anything.

548
00:47:31.580 --> 00:47:37.769
Gary Young: I mean, there are problems within the town, and, you know, you did sign up to come and help here, and.

549
00:47:37.770 --> 00:47:46.770
Kostadis Roussos: If you're going back to Lord Neverwinter while the town is still in a state of disrepair, it's not quite clear what… how he'll react. But far be it from me to tell you what to do.

550
00:47:54.060 --> 00:47:54.680
David Mendenhall: Okay.

551
00:47:55.200 --> 00:47:59.180
Kostadis Roussos: I mean, he's a lord of a large city, you're a third-level character.

552
00:47:59.330 --> 00:48:00.130
Kostadis Roussos: You know….

553
00:48:00.130 --> 00:48:01.350
David Mendenhall: We're not very… we're not very….

554
00:48:01.630 --> 00:48:03.079
Wade: We don't rate.

555
00:48:03.080 --> 00:48:06.810
David Mendenhall: We did agree to come here, and… Yes, and so….

556
00:48:06.810 --> 00:48:08.539
Kostadis Roussos: That's a good point.

557
00:48:08.540 --> 00:48:10.649
Gary Young: And he's like, you could go there.

558
00:48:11.040 --> 00:48:12.190
Kostadis Roussos: Any….

559
00:48:12.190 --> 00:48:13.500
David Mendenhall: It doesn't send you back.

560
00:48:14.030 --> 00:48:15.399
Kostadis Roussos: Or, or worse.

561
00:48:17.710 --> 00:48:23.350
Kostadis Roussos: Like, with, like, withdraw your tax-free status, and send you back.

562
00:48:26.730 --> 00:48:29.110
David Mendenhall: Alright, maybe we should go talk to Ser Kaelen.

563
00:48:30.310 --> 00:48:31.140
Kostadis Roussos: Right.

564
00:48:33.430 --> 00:48:34.390
Kostadis Roussos: Right.

565
00:48:34.630 --> 00:48:36.450
Kostadis Roussos: Let me just do something here…

566
00:48:38.980 --> 00:48:40.570
Kostadis Roussos: Like, something I need to do here.

567
00:48:54.260 --> 00:48:56.819
Kostadis Roussos: To just find something. Give me, give me one second…

568
00:49:22.580 --> 00:49:23.330
Kostadis Roussos: Hmm.

569
00:49:37.940 --> 00:49:39.460
Kostadis Roussos: Alright…

570
00:49:43.990 --> 00:49:46.479
Kostadis Roussos: Okay. Okey-dokey.

571
00:49:46.870 --> 00:49:50.919
Kostadis Roussos: Alright, so you go to, Ser Kaelen, yes?

572
00:49:52.280 --> 00:49:52.750
David Mendenhall: Should've came….

573
00:49:52.750 --> 00:49:56.809
Kostadis Roussos: Ser Kaelen is sitting there and is looking really happy to see you.

574
00:50:01.350 --> 00:50:04.429
Kostadis Roussos: Spider-man is also looking happy to see you.

575
00:50:06.410 --> 00:50:08.500
Wade: Why is he happy to see us?

576
00:50:08.670 --> 00:50:20.089
Kostadis Roussos: Well, because, you know, Vukradin played some music that was very successful in the pub. You know, he got to tell his story about how…

577
00:50:21.040 --> 00:50:27.340
Kostadis Roussos: … How… he got his nickname of Spider-Man.

578
00:50:28.120 --> 00:50:31.659
Kostadis Roussos: I mean, he, he, he, he… He likes… He likes it, man.

579
00:50:31.660 --> 00:50:32.430
Wade: Business, got it.

580
00:50:32.600 --> 00:50:43.670
Kostadis Roussos: you're good for business, you're working on the problems of the area. I mean, these are all good things. Why wouldn't… plus, you know, you're helping clear the area of evil agents.

581
00:50:44.870 --> 00:50:53.970
Kostadis Roussos: Right? So, like, from his perspective, why wouldn't he… … Alright.

582
00:50:55.070 --> 00:50:55.870
David Mendenhall: We're back!

583
00:50:56.200 --> 00:50:59.170
Kostadis Roussos: Oh, Ser Kaelen is delighted to see.

584
00:50:59.530 --> 00:51:12.899
Kostadis Roussos: He goes, I, Vukradin, how was your… were you able to achieve victory in… and secure the tower from its, the evil… the evil that was there?

585
00:51:13.430 --> 00:51:17.020
Kostadis Roussos: Baza's, was there evil there? Remember, we said there were 3 options.

586
00:51:18.050 --> 00:51:18.820
David Mendenhall: It was evil.

587
00:51:19.140 --> 00:51:20.329
Wade: There was Talos.

588
00:51:20.740 --> 00:51:26.709
Kostadis Roussos: Talos. Talos. He goes, Paul pauses and says, Now that is of grave concern.

589
00:51:27.500 --> 00:51:35.089
Kostadis Roussos: Talos? Was it one… was it… was it… was… there was… was there anything else strange about Talos? Was Cleric of Talos?

590
00:51:35.640 --> 00:51:37.269
Wade: He had a hole in his chest.

591
00:51:38.180 --> 00:51:39.529
Kostadis Roussos: A hole in his chest.

592
00:51:39.530 --> 00:51:39.950
Wade: Yeah.

593
00:51:39.950 --> 00:51:45.649
David Mendenhall: He hadn't used his… he had illuminated his heart and used it to light the lighthouse.

594
00:51:45.650 --> 00:51:53.590
Kostadis Roussos: Because this is very strange. A typical shaman of Talos could not do such things. There's some hidden force deeper here.

595
00:51:54.670 --> 00:51:56.030
David Mendenhall: There were hockeys, too.

596
00:51:57.130 --> 00:52:01.499
Wade: Yeah, we didn't find any greater force there that we noticed.

597
00:52:01.500 --> 00:52:05.449
Kostadis Roussos: Yes, well, there's… who knows what's going on? There's so many different…

598
00:52:05.830 --> 00:52:19.789
Kostadis Roussos: This… ever since the end of the War of the Giants and the War of the Dragons, this whole area's been in a state of chaos. Many of my brethren died fighting the dragons. Several died fighting the barbarians. But, sorry, the….

599
00:52:20.440 --> 00:52:28.429
David Mendenhall: Something happened, though, along the way to the tower that I need to ask you about.

600
00:52:28.430 --> 00:52:29.470
Kostadis Roussos: He goes, what?

601
00:52:30.600 --> 00:52:31.729
David Mendenhall: We were ambushed.

602
00:52:32.710 --> 00:52:35.860
Kostadis Roussos: He goes… My goodness. By whom?

603
00:52:38.360 --> 00:52:41.290
David Mendenhall: Someone who knew… someone who knew we were coming.

604
00:52:41.690 --> 00:52:46.010
Kostadis Roussos: … he denies… he denies it.

605
00:52:46.990 --> 00:52:49.070
Kostadis Roussos: And he's telling the truth, actually.

606
00:52:49.690 --> 00:52:53.380
David Mendenhall: But who would have known that we… but who would have known that we were coming?

607
00:52:55.540 --> 00:52:56.280
Kostadis Roussos: I don't see….

608
00:52:56.280 --> 00:52:58.000
Gary Young: Like, we've been very secretive.

609
00:52:58.000 --> 00:53:05.929
Kostadis Roussos: Yeah, Ser Kaelen goes, let me see. He raises his hand. Who knew that these individuals were willing to go to the Tower of the…

610
00:53:06.720 --> 00:53:08.230
Kostadis Roussos: In this bar.

611
00:53:08.780 --> 00:53:16.410
Kostadis Roussos: People raise their head. Somebody goes, we were taking bets on whether all four would come back, or whether they would ditch the barn.

612
00:53:16.900 --> 00:53:19.230
Wade: Anyway, shouldn't we get a cut of those bets?

613
00:53:22.610 --> 00:53:25.049
David Mendenhall: I think… I think we're gonna need to be more secretive.

614
00:53:25.050 --> 00:53:28.849
Kostadis Roussos: Spider… Spider-Man… Spider-Man points to a budding pool.

615
00:53:30.420 --> 00:53:32.140
David Mendenhall: What are you guys betting we'll do next?

616
00:53:32.920 --> 00:53:34.090
Kostadis Roussos: ….

